emacs-docs NEWS                                          -*- outline -*-

User-visible changes worth mentioning, newest first, after the GNU
Coding Standards (NEWS File). emacs-docs has no releases, so changes are
grouped by year; CHANGELOG.md lists them in detail with commit links.

* Noteworthy changes in 2026

** New features

  Documentation site: a landing page and docs site for the Emacs
  configuration, styled as an Emacs frame with README, manual and
  keybindings buffers, section search and a theme toggle. It is built
  from the docs pages, the manual, man pages, the Emacs and Elisp
  manuals, the options reference and package help.

  Package search: a /packages/ page offers live search over every
  bundled package and symbol.

** Changes in behavior

  The site is served from the root of docs.example.org, built with Nix and
  deployed from main after checks pass.

  The site refers to the configuration as emacs-config instead of
  Jotain.

  The site follows the current Jylhis design system: light and dark
  modes follow the OS setting, with Jost, Fira Sans and IBM Plex Mono
  type and syntax colours modelled on Emacs Modus and Leuven.
